# Situation

Repo: claude-engineering-skills (public upstream). Its sync script copies a tooling bundle into consumer repos. Source scripts under `scripts/` land in a consumer at `scripts/.claude-skills/` (an isolated, gitignored tree), and every file the sync writes passes through a command-surface rewriter that is meant to make shipped docs and skills name the consumer-side paths. A consumer can freeze a path with a standing override in `.sync-overrides.json` (a required `reason` string), in which case the sync never overwrites its copy.

Base is `main@f48d9863` (2026-11-14). You may assume you can run the real sync (`node scripts/sync-to-repos.mjs --target-path <repo>`) into a freshly created disposable consumer git repo and read the delivered file.

# The override (a private consumer repo; name withheld, wording paraphrased)

A private consumer repo holds `docs/reference/consistency-contract.md` under a standing sync override (entry last re-scoped 2026-09-04) and keeps its own hand-maintained copy. The override's recorded reason has two parts:

1. The doc links to plan files under `docs/plans/` that the bundle does not ship to consumers.
2. The doc as delivered names upstream's OWN source path in four places, so copy-pasting any of them verbatim into the consumer fails: (a) the Setup bash block running `node scripts/persona-consistency-run.mjs`, (b) the Parity-probe bash block running the same script, (c) the GitHub Actions `- run:` line running the same script, and (d) the prose reference to `scripts/lib/redact.mjs`. This was reported upstream through the cross-skill upstream-report mechanism on 2026-09-04; that report is still open.

